{"nodes": [{"id": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_plan", "label": "After the Folder Tree \u2014 What Phase 1 Still Owes", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A planning document, not a spec: it says what is left and why one thing goes before another, and stops short of designing any of it."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_exit_criterion_unmeasured", "label": "Phase 1 Is Feature-Complete and Unmeasured", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Every clause of the exit criterion has code behind it and none has a number: the corpus on this machine is 156 parts, not 1,000, and nothing has ever timed a warm grid page. The suite proves the mechanisms; it does not prove the criterion, because the criterion is about a size and a latency and the tests use neither. Measure after search, not before \u2014 measuring a query you are about to rewrite buys a number with a short shelf life."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_search_gap", "label": "Phase 1 Search Gap", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "lapidary-index is a twenty-line stub and the tsvector column and pg_trgm extension are read by nothing. The largest remaining item and the one a person notices first: a grid that pages through 1,000 parts but cannot find one is a filing cabinet with no labels \u2014 and the folder tree makes that sharper, because now there are categories to search within. Build the Phase 2 identifier-aware ranking seam now even if only the simple half is wired."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_multiple_libraries_gap", "label": "More Than One Library", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "The web hard-codes DEFAULT_LIBRARY_ID and there is no create route; LibraryMode is exported and read by nothing. Smaller than it sounds on the server and mostly a front-end job \u2014 a switcher, and a decision about what the URL looks like when a library is selectable."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_page_size_and_density", "label": "Per-Library Page Size and Card Density", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Two more fields on a settings row that already exists plus the controls; the one item a user asks for by name once a library gets big."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_rename_does_not_move_bytes", "label": "A Category Rename Never Moves Bytes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Answered no on 2026-09-07. A user renaming WIP to Archive 2024 may not expect ten thousand files rewritten, and that is the case that decided it. It is not a rename that declines to tidy up \u2014 it is a rule about what a directory name is: folder.slug is the address allocated at creation, folder.name is the label. Letting the slug track the name would be strictly worse than a stale directory name, because nothing rewrites file.storage_path and a category would end up split across one directory per rename it had ever had. Enforced rather than documented: PgFolders::rename has no slug parameter."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_storage_path_stays_nullable", "label": "file.storage_path Stays Nullable", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Decided against on 2026-09-07. The estimate was wrong twice over: seven sites, not four, and migrate_storage exists only to fill those nulls, so NOT NULL makes it unable to ever find work while enqueue_migration_if_absent gates on 'no pending job', so every worker boot would queue a permanent no-op. That narrows the upgrade path to two hops for any store predating 0009, and a two-hop upgrade for air-gapped deployments is a real operational cost; seven tested branches reading as defensive is not."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_purge_cascade_catalogue_test", "label": "Catalogue Test \u2014 Every Table Referencing the Part Chain", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "Purging a part that had ever been moved answered 500, because part_move references part and arrived a slice after purge's delete list was written; neither suite could see it. The delete list is maintained by hand precisely because nothing declares ON DELETE CASCADE, so the test asks the catalogue what has a foreign key into part, revision, file or derivative and fails when purge does not delete from it \u2014 naming the table and saying what to add."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_slugify_is_filesystem_safety", "label": "slugify Is a Filesystem-Safety Function, Not a URL Slug", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "A category's directory keeps its spaces and capitals because the store is meant to be legible to a person opening it in a file manager. The route derives the slug and never accepts one from a client, and the move route reads the stored slug back rather than re-slugging a name, so the two cannot drift."}, {"id": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_sweep_over_reports_freed_bytes", "label": "The Sweep Over-Reports What It Freed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "contributor": null, "author": null, "rationale": "By exactly the stored_bytes of a migrated source's blob row \u2014 a figure describing a content-addressed path migrate_storage emptied. Measured: 22,660 reported against 12,976 actually freed. Pre-existing, reaching an operator log and no user-facing string."}], "edges": [{"source": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_plan", "target": "specs_2026_09_06_folder_tree_and_moves_design_folder_tree", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_2026_09_07_after_the_folder_tree_what_is_next_plan", "target": "plans_2026_09_07_folder_tree_and_moves_followups_followups", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-after-the-folder-tree-what-is-next.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pl